# Third plan: `Work.EKLC6Core.lintegral_growthFun_le_HcondSig_uij` (the `ℝ≥0∞` sandwich)

Requested statement: for a probability measure `μ`, `T = (aDiag t ·)`-invariant, a leaf-wise
system `ν` for `U = Uij hij`, `t i < t j`, and a conull `T`-descending plaque algebra `(Z, A)`
for `U`,

    ∫⁻ x, ENNReal.ofReal (growthFun U ν t x) ∂μ ≤ HcondSig μ A (comap T A).      (‡)

The *Bochner* form of (‡) is proved (`growth_le_HcondSig_mp`), but only modulo the integrability of
`growthFun`, so it does not help to *prove* integrability.  (‡) itself is the faithful statement.

Proof route.

1. `Work.EKLC6Core.lintegral_atomInfo_le_nocov` (proved, for an *arbitrary* horospherical `U`)
   already gives `∫⁻ x, ofReal (atomInfo A U ν t x) ∂μ ≤ HcondSig μ A (comap T A)`, where
   `atomInfo A U ν t x = -log ((ν x (shape A U x)).toReal / (ν x (shape (comap T A) U x)).toReal)`.
   So it suffices to prove

       ∫⁻ x, ofReal (growthFun U ν t x) ∂μ ≤ ∫⁻ x, ofReal (atomInfo A U ν t x) ∂μ.   (‡‡)

2. (‡‡) is Pisa 7.18/7.34 in `ℝ≥0∞` form.  The pointwise identity behind it is
   `atomInfo_ae_eq_single_alt` (proved in `Submission/Work/EKLC6Core/growth_le_HcondSig_mp.lean`):
   for a.e. `x`,
   `atomInfo x = φ (T x) - φ x + growthFun (T x)`,  `φ y := Real.log ((ν y (shape A U y)).toReal)`,
   i.e. the `atomInfo`'s are the Birkhoff sums of `growthFun` plus a telescoping boundary term.
   The boundary term is controlled by the *good times*: use
   `Work.EKLC6Core.exists_good_set_plaque` (proved) to get measurable `Y k`, `δ k > 0`, `R k > 0`
   with `V (δ k) ∩ U ⊆ shape A U y ⊆ V (R k)` for `y ∈ Y k`, and `∀ᵐ x, ∃ k, T^n x ∈ Y k` for
   infinitely many `n`.  At a good visit `T^n x ∈ Y k` one has `φ (T^n x) ≥ log (ν (V (δ k))) > 0`
   bounded below, so the telescoping boundary term along the orbit is bounded by
   `2 · max (log (1/δ k)) (...)`; Fatou (the positive part of the boundary term contributes the
   liminf) then yields (‡‡).  This is exactly the argument of the (now deleted) draft
   `lintegral_growthFun_le_lintegral_atomInfo.lean`, whose hypotheses `hY, hδ, hR, hvisit` are the
   output of `exists_good_set_plaque`.

3. Combine: (‡) = (1) after (2).
-/
